---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseStudy from '../../components/case/CaseStudy.astro';
import NotVerified from '../../components/case/NotVerified.astro';
import ModuleMap from '../../components/case/ModuleMap.astro';
import { projectRecords } from '../../data/portfolio';
import { koranco as korancoProject } from '../../data/registry';
import { PUBLIC_LINKS, SITE, caseMeta, SOCIAL_IMAGE } from '../../config/site';

const meta = caseMeta({
  name: korancoProject.name,
  summary: projectRecords.koranco.summary,
  image: '/social/koranco.png',
  imageAlt: 'Koranco Farms — attendance, produce and employee records, drawn as a module map.',
});
const { title, description, image, imageAlt } = meta;
const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CreativeWork',
  name: 'Koranco Farms MVP',
  description,
  url: new URL('/work/koranco/', Astro.site).href,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.name },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  {title}
  {description}
  {structuredData}
  {image}
  {imageAlt}
  imageWidth={SOCIAL_IMAGE.width}
  imageHeight={SOCIAL_IMAGE.height}
  ogType="article"
>
  <CaseStudy id="koranco">
    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <div style="view-transition-name: artifact-koranco">
        <ModuleMap />
      </div>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="problem">
      <p>
        Farm records were kept for the office, not the field. The job was to find out how
        production data actually got captured, then build something that survived the conditions on
        the farm.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three record types came out of that: who was present, what was produced, and who worked
        there. That is the whole scope of the MVP.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="contribution">
      <p>
        I built the three-module MVP in a six-week Ashesi Innovation Lab engagement, with the
        farm-operations side.
      </p>

      <ul class="role-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Offline-first field work</strong> — records are entered where connectivity is
          poor, not only at the office.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authentication and authorization</strong> — custom auth and role-based access on
          FastAPI and PostgreSQL, so a farmhand and a manager don’t see the same records.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A public face for the farm</strong> — a website for the business. Its address
          isn’t in the record, so it is described, not linked.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="case-note">
        The code isn’t public, so no schema or endpoint is described here. It would be a guess.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="decisions">
      <dl class="decision-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Follow the records, not a feature list</dt>
          <dd>
            The engagement produced three record types, so the MVP is organised around them, not
            around a generic suite of farm features.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Build for the connection the farm has</dt>
          <dd>
            Offline-first was the shape of the product, not a later optimisation. Records are
            captured in the field and reconciled after, so a dropped connection doesn’t stop the
            day’s work.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Decide access in the service</dt>
          <dd>
            Custom auth and role-based authorization live on the backend, next to the records they
            protect, not in the interface.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="result">
      <p>{projectRecords.koranco.result}</p>

      <dl class="case-states">
        <div>
          <dt>Delivered</dt>
          <dd><strong>Three modules, working.</strong> Attendance, produce and employees.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Deployment</dt>
          <dd><strong>None evidenced.</strong> No production deployment or rollout in the record.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="limits">
      <NotVerified
        lead="This account is built from the written record, not from a public build."
        items={[
          'No public repository, source excerpt or product screenshot',
          'No production deployment or farm-side adoption reported',
          'No measured operational outcome — no time saved, error rate or usage figure',
          'The farm’s website is described but not linked',
        ]}
      />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="sources">
      <ul class="case-sources">
        <li>
          <a href="/profile/">Profile and experience record</a>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">This site</span>
          <span>The Jul–Sep 2026 Innovation Lab role around it.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={PUBLIC_LINKS.resume}>Résumé (PDF)</a>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">PDF</span>
          <span>The supplied résumé record this account is drawn from.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="case-sources__plain">Innovation Lab brief</span>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">Not public</span>
          <span>The written project scope. No public link exists.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>


    </Fragment>
  </CaseStudy>
</BaseLayout>

